yoyo now refuses the retired GitHub Models provider with a message that says why, and the setup wizard and README no longer offer it. Committed as 60546025 with the title "Part of #1166", not "Fixes".

What changed
• Startup refusal (`src/providers.rs`): --provider github or provider = "github" with no base URL now exits with code 2 before any network call. The message gives the retirement date (2026-07-30), the changelog URL, and two alternatives: --provider openrouter, or --provider custom --base-url <url>. If a base URL is given, it still runs, because the user picked an endpoint.
• REPL (`src/commands.rs`): /provider github was a separate path that didn't go through the startup check. It now uses the same refusal and leaves the session's provider and model unchanged (about 7 lines).
• Setup wizard (`src/setup.rs`): the GitHub Models row is gone, so Custom moves from 14 to 13. I updated the existing tests to the new numbering and added wizard_does_not_offer_retired_github_models, which checks that "github" isn't accepted by name or number and that "14" is now past the end of the list. No tests were deleted.
• README: GitHub Models is off the provider list. docs/src had no mentions of it.

Checked with the built binary (env -i HOME=/tmp/gh GITHUB_TOKEN=x):
```
error: provider 'github' (GitHub Models) was retired by GitHub on 2026-07-30 and no longer answers requests (https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-30-github-models-is-now-retired)
for the same model families use: --provider openrouter
for an OpenAI-compatible server use: --provider custom --base-url <url>
exit=2
```
The same refusal appeared when the provider came from .yoyo.toml. With --base-url http://127.0.0.1:9/v1, it ran and got "connection refused" from that address, which shows the request went to the URL the user gave.

Build, all tests (0 failures, size gates included), clippy with -D warnings, and fmt --check pass.

